Overview
The Random Hadith Generator is a web-based application that displays random Islamic hadiths to users by fetching data from an external API endpoint.
Key Characteristics:

RESTful API integration
Real-time data fetching
Audio playback for hadith recitation

High-Level Architecture
mermaidgraph TD
    A[User Browser] --> B[index.html]
    B --> C[script.js]
    C --> D[Vercel API]
    D --> E[Hadith Database]
The system uses a client-server architecture where JavaScript fetches hadith data from the Vercel API endpoint.
Core Components

HTML Interface - Basic page structure
JavaScript Controller - Handles API requests
Stylesheet - Visual styling

Data Flow
When the user clicks "New Hadith":

JavaScript calls fetchRandomHadith()
API request sent to Vercel endpoint
Data returned and displayed on page

Code Implementation
Main API Function
File: script.js
javascriptasync function fetchRandomHadith() {
  try {
    const response = await fetch('https://random-hadith-generator.vercel.app/bukhari/');
    const data = await response.json();
    displayHadith(data.data.hadith_english, data.data.header, data.data.book);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error fetching Hadith:', error);
  }
}
Explanation: This function fetches hadith data from the Vercel API and passes it to the display function.
Display Function
File: script.js
javascriptfunction displayHadith(hadith, narrator, book) {
  hadithElement.innerText = hadith;
  narratorElement.innerText = narrator;
  bookElement.innerText = book;
}
Explanation: Updates the page with the hadith content.
Audio Playback
File: script.js
javascriptsoundButton.addEventListener('click', function() {
  const utterance = new SpeechSynthesisUtterance(hadithElement.innerText);
  utterance.lang = 'ar-SA';
  window.speechSynthesis.speak(utterance);
});
Explanation: Plays the hadith text using the browser's speech synthesis API.
Integration Points
External API: https://random-hadith-generator.vercel.app/bukhari/
Returns JSON format:
json{
  "data": {
    "hadith_english": "...",
    "header": "...",
    "book": "..."
  }
}
Font Services: Google Fonts CDN for typography
Configuration
Set the API endpoint in your environment:
bashAPI_ENDPOINT=https://random-hadith-generator.vercel.app/bukhari/
Monitoring and Operations
Error logging to console:
javascriptconsole.error('Error fetching Hadith:', error);
The system logs API errors for debugging purposes.
